439
00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.460
The Optimizer proposes up to three ideas.

440
00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.460
The Guardian vetoes.

441
00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.440
And in the first cycle,

442
00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.710
the Evaluator almost always says:

443
00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.880
insufficient sample, continue.

444
00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.080
That’s not a failure.

445
00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.080
It was the answer in the clinic’s

446
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:41.740
first cycle.

447
00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:43.700
The first cycle gives you the first

448
00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.820
history entry and the first veto with

449
00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.160
a reason.

450
00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.620
Watch out for a common mistake:

451
00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.520
twelve proposals do not prove that Tuesdays

452
00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:53.620
convert better.

453
00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.540
Record it and wait for the sample

454
00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.600
size that proves it.

455
00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.500
If B is ahead in week two,

456
00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.920
