470
00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.020
Marcos’s card will have the same shape:

471
00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:26.880
resolution from fifty-five to

472
00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.480
sixty-one percent, one hundred eighty on each

473
00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:32.240
side, and a cost of sixty-two out

474
00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:33.160
of eighty reais.

475
00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.980
And be careful:

476
00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.500
stopping the test before the sample size

477
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.020
proves anything because B is ahead is

478
00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.440
the most common way to promote noise.

479
00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.980
Approving one card a week for months

480
00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.900
is the loop working as promised.

481
00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.360
Now, the course formula:

482
00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:52.380
execution times evidence times experimentation times memory

483
00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:54.040
equals evolution.

484
00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.820
It’s multiplication, not addition:

485
00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:59.040
any factor at zero makes

486
00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.220
the result zero.

487
00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.620
Track One showed execution.

488
00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.520
Track Two gave you evidence.

489
00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:07.800
Tracks Two and Four gave you experimentation,

490
00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.770
and Track Three gave you memory.

491
00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:13.200
Paulo has plenty of execution and zero

492
00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:15.700
memory: no one knows what’s already been

493
00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.240
